    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "Feature Overview",
      "Anchor": "feature-overview",
      "SectionPath": [
        "Feature Overview"
      ],
      "Text": "The Organization Photos API returns photos uploaded by organization admins to be displayed on organization pages (including Companies, Schools, and Showcase pages). These photos can appear in various sections of the organization\u0027s page, such as the Photos section on Life Pages (Targeted Content pages) or other media sections.",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "Feature Overview",
      "Anchor": "feature-overview",
      "SectionPath": [
        "Feature Overview"
      ],
      "Text": "Organization admins can upload photos through the LinkedIn organization page management interface to showcase their workplace, culture, events, and team. These photos are then available via this API for data portability purposes.",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "Product Terminology",
      "Anchor": "product-terminology",
      "SectionPath": [
        "Feature Overview",
        "Product Terminology"
      ],
      "Text": "This API relates to the following LinkedIn features:",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "Product Terminology",
      "Anchor": "product-terminology",
      "SectionPath": [
        "Feature Overview",
        "Product Terminology"
      ],
      "Text": "Organization Photos - Refers to photos uploaded to organization pages. This is the current term used for such images.\nLife Pages - Also known as \u0022Targeted Content\u0022 pages, where these photos can be displayed.\nCompany Pages - Now referred to as \u0022Organization Pages,\u0022 which include companies, schools, and showcase pages.",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "Product Terminology",
      "Anchor": "product-terminology",
      "SectionPath": [
        "Feature Overview",
        "Product Terminology"
      ],
      "Text": "If you\u0027re looking for photos displayed on your organization\u0027s Life Page or Company Page, this is the correct API to use.",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "Prerequisites",
      "Anchor": "prerequisites",
      "SectionPath": [
        "How to Use This API?",
        "Prerequisites"
      ],
      "Text": "To use this API, the authenticated member must have one of the following organization page roles:",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "Prerequisites",
      "Anchor": "prerequisites",
      "SectionPath": [
        "How to Use This API?",
        "Prerequisites"
      ],
      "Text": "ADMINISTRATOR\nCONTENT_ADMINISTRATOR",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "Prerequisites",
      "Anchor": "prerequisites",
      "SectionPath": [
        "How to Use This API?",
        "Prerequisites"
      ],
      "Text": "See Organization Access Control for more information on company page roles.",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "Obtaining Organization Photo URNs",
      "Anchor": "obtaining-organization-photo-urns",
      "SectionPath": [
        "How to Use This API?",
        "Obtaining Organization Photo URNs"
      ],
      "Text": "To retrieve organization photos, you need to construct an organizationPhotoUrn. There are two primary ways to obtain the necessary information:",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "Obtaining Organization Photo URNs",
      "Anchor": "obtaining-organization-photo-urns",
      "SectionPath": [
        "How to Use This API?",
        "Obtaining Organization Photo URNs"
      ],
      "Text": "From Targeted Content (Life Pages) - If you want to retrieve photos displayed on a Life Page, first call the Organization Targeted Contents API to get the targeted content data. The response includes a photosSection field containing an array of OrganizationPhotoUrn values that you can use directly with this API.\n\nUsing Available Endpoints - Call the Organization Photos API\u0027s GET or BATCH_GET method with:\n\nThe organization URN (obtained from Organizations API)\nThe specific photo ID (if known from previous uploads or content management)",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "Available Methods",
      "Anchor": "available-methods",
      "SectionPath": [
        "How to Use This API?",
        "Available Methods"
      ],
      "Text": "The service provides the following methods:",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "Available Methods",
      "Anchor": "available-methods",
      "SectionPath": [
        "How to Use This API?",
        "Available Methods"
      ],
      "Text": "GET - Returns a single photo based on the unique organizationPhotoUrn.\nBATCH_GET - Returns multiple photos for the given organizationPhotoUrn values.",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
